    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.keymap\n\n### Description\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/17b4b556-ee7a-4168-a9df-b94398d3c9ac\n\n<details>\n<summary>init.lua</summary>\n\n```lua\n---@diagnostic disable: undefined-global\nlocal function setup_deps(path_to_site)\n  local mini_path = path_to_site .. \"pack/deps/start/mini.nvim\"\n  if not vim.uv.fs_stat(mini_path) then\n    vim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\n    vim.fn.system({ \"git\", \"clone\", \"--filter=blob:none\", \"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim\", mini_path })\n    vim.cmd(\"packadd mini.nvim | helptags ALL\")\n    vim.cmd('echo \"Installed `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\n  end\n  require(\"mini.deps\").setup({ path = { package = path_to_site } })\nend\nsetup_deps(vim.fn.stdpath(\"data\") .. \"/site/\")\n\nvim.o.completeopt = \"menuone,noselect,fuzzy,nosort\"\nvim.o.shortmess = \"CFOSWaco\"\nvim.g.mapleader = \" \"\nMiniDeps.now(function()\n  require(\"mini.basics\").setup()\n  require(\"mini.notify\").setup()\n  require(\"mini.icons\").setup()\n  MiniIcons.tweak_lsp_kind()\n\n  require(\"mini.snippets\").setup({\n    --\n  })\n  require(\"mini.completion\").setup({ lsp_completion = { auto_setup = false, source_func = \"omnifunc\" } })\n\n  MiniDeps.add(\"neovim/nvim-lspconfig\")\n  vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"LspAttach\", {\n    group = vim.api.nvim_create_augroup(\"my.lsp\", {}),\n    callback = function(args) vim.bo[args.buf].omnifunc = \"v:lua.MiniCompletion.completefunc_lsp\" end,\n  })\n  vim.lsp.config(\"*\", { capabilities = MiniCompletion.get_lsp_capabilities() })\n  vim.lsp.config(\"lua_ls\", {\n    settings = {\n      Lua = {\n        completion = { callSnippet = \"Replace\" },\n        diagnostics = { workspaceDelay = -1 }, -- don't analyze\n        runtime = { version = \"LuaJIT\", path = vim.split(package.path, \";\") },\n        telemetry = { enable = false },\n        workspace = { library = { vim.env.VIMRUNTIME, \"${3rd}/luv/library\" } },\n      },\n    },\n  })\n  vim.lsp.enable({ \"lua_ls\" })\n\n  local map_multistep = require(\"mini.keymap\").map_multistep\n\n  local tab_steps = {\n    \"minisnippets_next\",\n    \"minisnippets_expand\",\n    -- \"pmenu_next\",\n    \"jump_after_tsnode\",\n    \"jump_after_close\",\n  }\n  map_multistep(\"i\", \"<Tab>\", tab_steps)\n\n  local shifttab_steps = {\n    \"minisnippets_prev\",\n    -- \"pmenu_prev\",\n    \"jump_before_tsnode\",\n    \"jump_before_open\",\n  }\n  map_multistep(\"i\", \"<S-Tab>\", shifttab_steps)\nend)\n\n```\n</details>\n\nI added a mapping based on the \"extra smart\" mappings as described in the [help](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c39f7f506939f065d0d1af237e2ea3f252edd3d4/doc/mini-keymap.txt#L104)\n\n```lua\nlocal steps_ctrl_l = { \"minisnippets_next\", \"jump_after_tsnode\", \"jump_after_close\" }\n```\n\nI removed the `pmenu` step in order to keep the `<c-p>/<c-n>` navigation. However as the pmenu is not \"captured\" in the steps, it remains open when \"jumping before/after\".\n\nIn my [config](https://github.com/abeldekat/nvim_pde/blob/cf61da0cfee2810944f7bddf2ae8f1feb4d1c331/lua/ak/config/editing/snippets.lua#L26) I added the following to solve the problem:\n\n```lua\nlocal no_pmenu = { -- make sure pmenu is closed after snippets and before jump\n  condition = function() return vim.fn.pumvisible() == 1 end,\n  action = function()\n    vim.schedule(function() -- see mini.snippets, H.hide_completion\n      if vim.fn.mode() == \"i\" then vim.cmd('silent noautocmd call complete(col(\".\"), [])') end\n    end)\n    return false\n  end,\n}\nlocal steps_ctrl_l = { \"minisnippets_next\", no_pmenu, \"jump_after_tsnode\", \"jump_after_close\" }\nMiniKeymap.map_multistep(\"i\", \"<C-l>\", steps_ctrl_l)\nlocal steps_ctrl_h = { \"minisnippets_prev\", no_pmenu, \"jump_before_tsnode\", \"jump_before_open\" }\nMiniKeymap.map_multistep(\"i\", \"<C-h>\", steps_ctrl_h)\n\n```\n\nThe problem does not occur when using `blink` instead of `mini.completion`.\n\nDo you think a builtin `no_pmenu` step would be appropriate in `mini.keymap`? If so, I would like to create a PR.",
